    "https://usfca.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/USF-Hilltop-Campus/Teaching-Professor--Department-of-Chemistry--University-of-San-Francisco_R0012773": {
      "title": "Teaching Professor, Department of Chemistry, University of San Francisco",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nJob Title: Teaching Professor, Department of Chemistry, University of San Francisco Job Summary: The Department of Chemistry at the University of San Francisco invites applications for a one-year full-time Teaching Professor position at the Assistant Professor level, to begin August 2027. This is a teaching-focused position with no research responsibilities. Our ACS-certified department offers a BS in Chemistry, a BS with Biochemistry concentration, a BS with Medicinal/Synthetic Chemistry concentration, and a thesis-based MS in Chemistry. The department is supported by a full-time stockroom manager, organic lab coordinator/NMR manager, instrumentation specialists, and a science safety officer. Full Job Description: Job Responsibilities: The successful candidate will teach General Chemistry and Organic Chemistry lecture and laboratory courses, and may also be asked to teach Medicinal Chemistry. A full-time teaching assignment consists of a combination of lecture sections (4 units each) and laboratory sections (2 units each) totaling 12 teaching units per semester. The successful candidate will also be expected to engage in service to the d epartment and college.   Minimum Qualifications : Applicants should hold a Ph.D. (or expect to complete their Ph.D. by August 202 7 ) in Chemistry or a closely related field. This position requires a commitment to excellence in teaching within a culturally diverse environment. In addition, a strong record of teaching at the university level, evidence of scholarship, and an understanding of and commitment to supporting the mission of the University of San Francisco are required. Applicants should submit: a cover letter summarizing interests and qualifications, a curriculum vitae, a statement of teaching philosophy and experience, evidence of teaching ability (e.g., sample syllabi, student and/or peer teaching evaluations), and three letters of recommendation (requested upon submission of application) . Questions can be address ed to chemistrysearch@usfca.edu . Priority will be given to applications received by October 1 , 202 6 .   We invite candidates to find out more about the Department of Chemistry at https://www.usfca.edu/arts-sciences/programs/undergraduate/chemistry/program-overview . In addition all new faculty have access to support from the Center for Teaching Excellence and the Center for Research, Artistic and Scholarly Excellence . Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Rate: Salary Salary Range : $103,184.83 - $113,633.96 annualized; commensurate with experience"
    },
    "https://usfca.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/USF-Hilltop-Campus/Professor_R0012633": {
      "title": "Professor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-23\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title: Professor Job Summary: The School of Nursing and Health Professions at the University of San Francisco invites nominations and applications for a tenure-track faculty position specializing in Maternal-Child Health, Pediatric and/or Medical-Surgical/Geriatric nursing for prelicensure/graduate nursing programs at the Hilltop Campus located in the heart of San Francisco. Full Job Description: Successful candidates will be expected to engage in didactic and clinical teaching, scholarship, and service that will contribute to the university and profession. They will develop and teach courses in the area(s) of Maternal-Child Health, Pediatric and/or Medical-Surgical/Geriatric nursing, be responsible for producing scholarship commensurate with the requirements of tenure, and contribute to the advancement of the School of Nursing and Health Professions through student advisement, service on committees and participation in the broader university and disciplinary communities. Minimum Qualifications:  ·        An earned doctoral degree in nursing or related area and a BSN or MSN if doctoral degree is not in nursing.  ·        Upon hire, the faculty member must be licensed as a registered nurse in California.  ·        One year of full-time direct patient care experience in Maternal-Child Health, Pediatric and/or Medical-Surgical/Geriatric nursing within the last 5 years. ·        A record of accomplishments in teaching, scholarship and services appropriate for appointment at the rank of a tenure track assistant professor or associate professor. The successful applicant will receive the appropriate rank and title based on university standards, including any prior service in a tenure-earning position, and consistent with the university collective bargaining agreement ·        A strong commitment to teaching and scholarship, experience and willingness to work in a culturally diverse environment and an understanding of and commitment to support the mission of the University. We invite candidates to learn more about the program located in the heart of San Francisco https://www.usfca.edu/nursing.   Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Rate: Salary Salary Range : Professor, Step 4 - $153,123.68"
